# V60/V70 and System 32 oracle for OutRunners, Rad Rally, Rad Mobile and F1
# Exhaust Note, Jurassic Park, SegaSonic and Golden Axe: The Revenge of
# Death Adder. Applies on top of the Model 1/2 cores repo patch
# 0006-model1-v60-trace.patch (M1TRACE_*):
# adds M1TRACE_PCLOG_EVERY, M1TRACE_FRAMES (one line per screen 0 update, both
# System 32 and Multi 32), M1TRACE_DUMP=DIR (each frame as DIR/f<n>.ppm) and
# M1TRACE_REPLAY (input replay keyed on start_of_vblank_int; the format
# s32_trace --replay reads). F1 Exhaust Note's second board ("subpcb")
# writes M1TRACE_SUB_PCLOG, M1TRACE_SUB_PCS and M1TRACE_SUB_FRAMES, and its
# replay ports are SUB_P1_A and so on; the main board steps the replay.
# SegaSonic's trackballs replay as TRACKX1..TRACKY3 (12-bit counts) through
# a hook in upd4701.cpp; EXTRA1-3 (the 4-player boards' 8255) replay too.
# M1TRACE_V25_PCLOG writes the V25's every 256th instruction (PC and
# registers; Golden Axe: The Revenge of Death Adder's protection CPU).
# Build: make SUBTARGET=s32 SOURCES=src/mame/sega/segas32.cpp USE_QTDEBUG=0

